  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "In electrolytic purification cathode is of pure metal and anode is of impure metal. At anode: $\\mathrm{M} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{M}^{\\mathrm{n}+}+\\mathrm{n} \\overline{\\mathrm{e}}$\nAt cathode: $\\mathrm{M}^{\\mathrm{n}+}+\\mathrm{n} \\overline{\\mathrm{e}} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{M}$.\nThe pure metal is thus deposited at cathode.",
